# ==============================================================================
# Online Boutique - Trivy Vulnerability Exception Policy & Ignore List
# ==============================================================================
#
# POLICY & GOVERNANCE:
# 1. Zero Undocumented Waivers:
#    Any CVE added to this file must contain an accompanying comment block
#    stating the exact reason for the waiver, impact analysis, ticket ID,
#    and expiration date.
#
# 2. Required Fields per Exception:
#    # CVE-YYYY-XXXXX
#    # - Reason: [Detailed technical justification why the vulnerability is not exploitable]
#    # - Context: [Service(s) affected, runtime environment, network reachability]
#    # - Ticket: [Azure DevOps Work Item / GitHub Issue reference]
#    # - Expiration: [YYYY-MM-DD - maximum waiver validity 90 days]
#    # - ApprovedBy: [Name / Role]
#
# 3. Patch Availability:
#    Vulnerabilities with an available upstream fix SHOULD NOT be ignored.
#    Prioritize upgrading the base image or updating application dependencies.
#    Use --ignore-unfixed for flaws where no remediation currently exists.
#
# 4. Expiration Lifecycle:
#    Expired exceptions will be purged during regular sprint security reviews.
#
# ==============================================================================
# ACTIVE EXCEPTIONS:
# (Currently empty - All base images and dependencies are free of CRITICAL CVEs)
# ==============================================================================
#
# Example Template:
# # CVE-2026-99999
# # - Reason: Flaw in glibc regex parser, not reachable in pure-Go static binary
# # - Context: frontend service distroless container
# # - Ticket: #27
# # - Expiration: 2026-12-31
# # - ApprovedBy: SecOps Lead
# CVE-2026-99999
